From f3856ee9b198a3f6f575b9ce53b8a8d3ae076721 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 05:19:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(video): brand kits steer topic videos end to end
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A topic video can now carry a brand kit, and every part of the pipeline
that has a brand-shaped decision to make consults it:

- Script: the kit's voice traits, audience, CTA style, and restricted
  terms become a "Brand voice" block in the script prompt, so the
  narration sounds like the brand instead of generic AI copy.
- Captions: the first parseable brand colour, darkened for contrast
  behind white text, becomes the caption stroke.
- Frames: the kit's icon mark (or primary logo) is stamped top-right at
  ~7% frame height and 85% opacity, clear of both caption styles.

Branding is opt-in and strictly fail-soft. No brandKitId means the
render is byte-for-byte what it was before; a missing kit, unparseable
colour, or unloadable logo just skips that one touch and the video still
ships. Only /objects/ logo paths are watermarked — an external logo URL
would mean fetching an arbitrary host at render time, so those are
ignored.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
